# Lab 04 – Implement Virtual Networking

## Objectives
- Create and configure virtual networks and subnets.
- Establish VNet peering between VNets.
- Test private connectivity across VNets using virtual machines.

## Tasks Completed
- Created resource group **az104-rg4** in East US.
- Deployed **az104-vnet1** (10.30.0.0/20) with subnets:  
  - subnet0 (10.30.0.0/24)  
  - subnet1 (10.30.1.0/24)  
  - subnet2 (10.30.2.0/24)  
- Deployed **az104-vnet2** (10.31.0.0/20) with subnet0 (10.31.0.0/24).
- Configured **VNet peering** between `az104-vnet1` and `az104-vnet2`.
- Deployed one VM into each VNet and verified **ping connectivity** using private IPs.

## Key Takeaways
- VNets allow segmentation of address space into multiple subnets.
- VNet peering enables cross-VNet communication without public IPs.
- Connectivity was successfully verified with VM-to-VM pings.

